|~ `::tag`, the kind of a tag name, its constructor and its refusal, and
   the verbs that live on a tag name: the comparisons of tag names,
   `manifest` and `runLaws`. ~|

::tag
  |~~ The kind of a tag name, `::Kind` taken as a value. A tag is the name
      of a kind, the interpretation of the value it stands on, and the
      model of the language hangs on it: a value carries its kind as the
      tag over it, a name finds its verb through that tag, and the tag
      names the page of the kind, so `type | doc` reads the page of a
      value's kind. Tags stack over any payload and read from the outside
      in; behaviour does not travel with a value, it is found again
      through the tag wherever the value goes. A tag names apart from a
      keyword, so `:d` and `::d` are two names; a tag no step declared is
      declared where it is first used, and its declaration says so.
      ::snippet~(::Box::Crate{:a 1} | type) answers `::Box`, and
      ::snippet~(::qlang | manifest) lists the kinds.
      ::link~(::qlang | doc :values)

      ~(::Box | type | eq ::tag)
      ~(::Even {:impl ~(if (eq 2) ~(/) ~(!{:reason :odd}))} | ::Even(3) !| /reason | eq :odd)
      ~(::tag::Box | eq ::Box)
      ~(5 | type | doc | type | eq ::doc)
      ~(:d ::verb~(mul 60) | ::d {:impl ~({:s /})} | [(10 | d) (::d(10) | payload)] | eq [600 {:s 10}])
      ~(::Unbound[1] | type | spec | /declarationOrigin | eq :implicit)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/tag}

::TagPayloadNotTagError
  |~~ `::tag…` payload must be a tag name.
      ~(
        ::tag:k
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::TagPayloadNotTagError ::keyword]
       )
  ~~|

|~ The comparisons of tag names. Each resides on `::qlang/tag`,
   the kind of the module that declares it, and compares two tag names
   by their names in the one order. ~|

:gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the tag the call
      gives.

      ~(::b | gt ::a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:than ::tag | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/gt})

:gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the tag
      the call gives.

      ~(::b | gte ::b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:than ::tag | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/gte})

:lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the tag the call
      gives.

      ~(::a | lt ::b | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:than ::tag | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/lt})

:lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      tag the call gives.

      ~(::a | lte ::a | eq true)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:than ::tag | :returns ::boolean | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/lte})

:manifest
  |~~ Asked of a noun, answers the set of what lies below it in
      the tree of names: the nouns under its path and the
      addresses of the verbs that live on it.
      ::snippet~(::qlang | manifest) lists the nouns of the core and of the hosts, `::number |
      manifest` the verbs of numbers, and a refusal is reached
      from the place it guards, `::number/add | spec | /throws`.
      For what one binding does reach for the axis trio
      (`::vec/count | source` / `| doc` / `| doc | laws`).

      ~(::number | manifest | has ::number/add)
      ~(::qlang | manifest | has ::vec)
      ~(::qlang | manifest * manifest | flat | has ::vec/count)
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::set | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/manifest})

::ManifestSubjectNotTagError
  |~~ `manifest` is asked of a noun, a tag name in the subject
      position.

      ~(
        5 | manifest
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::ManifestSubjectNotTagError ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:runLaws
  |~~ The results of the laws of the page of the declaration the tag
      name reads, a verb by its address among them, one `{:law :says
      :actual :ok :error}` per law, `:says` the caption of the claim the
      law proves. A keyword after it runs the laws of the member the
      name holds under it, a concept of the language among them.

      ~(::number/add | runLaws | first | /ok | eq true)
      ~(::qlang | runLaws :values | every ~(/ok))
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:anchor #[::keyword ::null] | :returns ::vec | ::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/runLaws})
